# Code owners for pappcorn/universe.
#
# GitHub requests these people as reviewers automatically on any PR touching
# the matching paths, which is what keeps the "every PR opens with an assignee
# and a reviewer" rule self-enforcing rather than something to remember.
#
# `main` is protected with `require_code_owner_reviews`, so a name here is not a
# suggestion — it is who can unblock a merge.
#
# ── Three maintainers, one of them an agent ──
# @cris-pappcorn is PappCorn's AI agent and a maintainer of this repo alongside
# its two humans. What that means in practice is spelled out in CONTRIBUTING.md
# and enforced by .github/workflows/cris-approve.yml: Cris only signs where its
# signature cannot be the thing that lets unreviewed code through. It never
# approves its own PRs, and never approves code from an author who is not
# already a code owner of everything they touched.

# Everything, by default.
*                        @ni500 @lcaloguerea @cris-pappcorn

# Connectors handle real credentials — keep both humans on them.
/packages/gmail-mcp/     @ni500 @lcaloguerea @cris-pappcorn
/packages/whatsapp-mcp/  @ni500 @lcaloguerea @cris-pappcorn

# ── The governance lock ──
# Humans only, on purpose. `/.github/` decides WHO approves and WHAT runs in CI,
# including cris-approve.yml itself. An agent that can approve changes to its own
# approver has no guard rail at all, so Cris is deliberately not an owner here.
# A PR touching this directory always waits for a human.
/.github/                @ni500 @lcaloguerea
